dy":"hmm yeah, do you prefer unlocking this? or you prefer pushing changes directly here? (@danielhanchen can add you to the unsloth org)","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5441422106/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5441675420","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742#issuecomment-5441675420","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27742","id":5441675420,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABRFlgnA","user":{"login":"ServeurpersoCom","id":4873680,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NzM2ODA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4873680?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom","html_url":"https://github.com/ServeurpersoCom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T15:51:27Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T15:51:27Z","body":"Re-tested at head on my prod box, both --kv-unified and --no-kv-unified: four concurrent requests plus an 8-way burst, no assert, and no compute buffer mismatch left in either mode.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5441675420/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5442190040","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742#issuecomment-5442190040","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27742","id":5442190040,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABRGE62A","user":{"login":"ngxson","id":7702203,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3MDIyMDM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7702203?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ngxson","html_url":"https://github.com/ngxson","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ngxson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ngxson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ngxson/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ngxson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ngxson/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ngxson/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ngxson/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ngxson/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ngxson/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T16:35:09Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T16:35:09Z","body":"Add `LazyChunkedTensor`, which simply the conversion code, and at the same time remove the need of a ~100GB temporary file during conversion: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742/commits/a510c82e17be1393936b2ed07c5e1ceee4b4e473\r\n\r\nI'm including this change as part of this PR (not a dedicated one), because this is the only model that can be benefit from it.\r\n\r\nAlso, https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27795 is merged and this PR is now rebased, appreciate if someone can validate end-to-end conversion + quantize pipeline. Memory usage should stay within limits now.\r\n\r\nAnd lastly, this PR should now be (fully) ready for review.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5442190040/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":2,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5442262487","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742#issuecomment-5442262487","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27742","id":5442262487,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABRGJV1w","user":{"login":"CISC","id":1629204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjkyMDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1629204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CISC","html_url":"https://github.com/CISC","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CISC/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CISC/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CISC/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CISC/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CISC/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CISC/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CISC/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CISC/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CISC/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T16:41:22Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T16:41:22Z","body":"> And lastly, this PR should now be (fully) ready for review.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/actions/runs/33093872290/job/98593564327?pr=27742#step:4:188","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5442262487/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5442334306","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742#issuecomment-5442334306","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27742","id":5442334306,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABRGNuYg","user":{"login":"ServeurpersoCom","id":4873680,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NzM2ODA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4873680?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom","html_url":"https://github.com/ServeurpersoCom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T16:47:24Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T16:47:24Z","body":"Quantization is underway with this PR rebased onto master...","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5442334306/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5442592196","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742#issuecomment-5442592196","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27742","id":5442592196,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABRGddxA","user":{"login":"solarkyle","id":30377578,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzc3NTc4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30377578?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/solarkyle","html_url":"https://github.com/solarkyle","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solarkyle/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solarkyle/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solarkyle/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solarkyle/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solarkyle/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solarkyle/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solarkyle/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solarkyle/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solarkyle/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T17:10:28Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T17:10:28Z","body":"Tuning data from a 16GB consumer card (RTX 5060 Ti / 9950X / 128GB DDR5-5600), UD-IQ4_XS, at `af1ffaf37` — in case the spec-type comparison is useful.\n\nMeasured on a copy-heavy code edit vs freeform prose, same server, one variable changed:\n\n```\n                code    prose   accept\nnone            20.75   21.12      —\nngram-mod       27.51   20.96   79.7%\nngram-simple    29.97      —    90.7%\nngram-map-k     30.02   21.24   92.0%\nngram-map-k4v   31.08      —    95.5%\nngram-cache     32.46   16.06   87.9%\n```\n\n`ngram-cache` is the fastest on repetitive output and the only one that regresses non-repetitive output (−24%). Acceptance rate doesn't track throughput — `ngram-map-k4v` accepts more drafts than `ngram-cache` and is slower.\n\n`--spec-draft-n-max` appears to be a no-op for the ngram types (2 / 4 / 6 / 8 / 12 all produced identical speed and identical acceptance). Not sure whether that's intended.\n\nTwo smaller notes: `--tensor-read-lazy auto` made no difference when combined with `--load-mode none` (30.59 vs 30.66 t/s, 89 GB RAM either way), which makes sense as the latter forces the model resident. And `--load-mode none` itself was a prefill-only lever here — ~45% better PP, no measurable effect on decode.\n\nsm_120 (consumer Blackwell) has been stable across ~40 server starts, CUDA 13.1 toolkit matching a 13.1 driver.\n\nFull data + harness scripts: https://github.com/solarkyle/qwen38-flashnext-16gb\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5442592196/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5442850368","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742#issuecomment-5442850368","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27742","id":5442850368,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABRGtOQA","user":{"login":"ggerganov","id":1991296,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTEyOTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1991296?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov","html_url":"https://github.com/ggerganov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T17:33:45Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T17:33:45Z","body":"> Also, #27795 is merged and this PR is now rebased, appreciate if someone can validate end-to-end conversion + quantize pipeline. Memory usage should stay within limits now.\r\n\r\nConverting here: https://github.com/ggml-org/convert/actions/runs/33095640791/job/98599706944","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5442850368/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":3},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5442902648","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742#issuecomment-5442902648","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27742","id":5442902648,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABRGwaeA","user":{"login":"mjungnickel18","id":41702029,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxNzAyMDI5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41702029?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjungnickel18","html_url":"https://github.com/mjungnickel18","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjungnickel18/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjungnickel18/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjungnickel18/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjungnickel18/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjungnickel18/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjungnickel18/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjungnickel18/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjungnickel18/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjungnickel18/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T17:38:20Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T17:41:49Z","body":"**Crash: QSA indexer cache desyncs from the attention cache when the server switches slots (LRU)**\n\nFound while running `llama-server` built from this branch (035e227) on Windows/CUDA (RTX 3090) with `unsloth/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GGUF:UD-Q3_K_XL`:\n\n```\nsrc/models/qwen4exp.cpp:285: GGML_ASSERT(mctx_idx->get_n_kv() == inp->mctx->get_attn()->get_n_kv() && \"the indexer cache must track the attention cache cell for cell\") failed\n```\n\n**Setup:** `llama-server -ngl 99 --n-cpu-moe 34 -ot ple_ngram_embd=CPU -c 65536` — note: default `--parallel`, i.e. 4 slots.\n\n**Repro:** send 4+ sequential chat completions. The first requests keep reusing slot 0 and work fine. As soon as the server picks a *different* slot via LRU, the next `launch_slot_` dies with the assert above. Log right before the crash:\n\n```\nslot      release: id  0 | task 403 | stop processing: n_tokens = 385, truncated = 0\nslot get_availabl: id  3 | task -1 | selected slot by LRU, t_last = 44464820\nslot launch_slot_: id  3 | task 755 | processing task, is_child = 0\nGGML_ASSERT(...) failed\n```\n\n100% reproducible for us on the first slot switch; single requests and same-slot sequences (including 35k-token prompts) are clean. Looks like the indexer cache isn't tracking the per-slot attention cache when a fresh slot is brought up.\n\n**Workaround:** `-np 1` (no slot switching) — stable for a full day of mixed use since.\n\nThis might not surface in typical PR testing because benchmarks against a fresh server tend to stay on slot 0. Happy to test a fix on our setup (Windows/CUDA, 3090, 96 GB RAM).","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5442902648/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"outdated"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5442928644","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742#issuecomment-5442928644","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27742","id":5442928644,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABRGyABA","user":{"login":"ServeurpersoCom","id":4873680,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NzM2ODA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4873680?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom","html_url":"https://github.com/ServeurpersoCom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T17:40:38Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T18:16:45Z","body":"The quantization is fine on my end :\r\n\r\n\"Converted and quantized end to end on a 96 GB box, no temp file and RSS never went past 2.6 GB during conversion. 354 GB BF16 in 21 min, then Q2_K with your --pure --tensor-type per_layer_token_embd.weight=q4_0 recipe, 337 GB down to 76 GB in 9 min. The engrams tensor lands at [59/1224], 97.7 GB to 27.5 GB. Loads and answers fine with the mmproj, 302 t/s prompt and 94 t/s generation on an RTX PRO 6000.\"","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5442928644/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5442950002","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742#issuecomment-5442950002","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27742","id":5442950002,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABRGzTcg","user":{"login":"ggerganov","id":1991296,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTEyOTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1991296?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov","html_url":"https://github.com/ggerganov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T17:42:33Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T17:42:33Z","body":"@mjungnickel18 You are building an old version. There is no problem on the latest version of this branch.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5442950002/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5443041531","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742#issuecomment-5443041531","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27742","id":5443041531,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABRG44-w","user":{"login":"solarkyle","id":30377578,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzc3NTc4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30377578?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/solarkyle","html_url":"https://github.com/solarkyle","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solarkyle/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solarkyle/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solarkyle/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solarkyle/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solarkyle/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solarkyle/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solarkyle/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solarkyle/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solarkyle/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T17:50:30Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T17:52:03Z","body":"Confirming @ggerganov on different hardware: the LRU slot-switch assert does not reproduce at `072f519f6`.\n\nRTX 5060 Ti 16GB (sm_120) / 9950X / 128GB DDR5-5600, Windows, UD-IQ4_XS, default `--parallel` (n_slots=4, kv_unified=true), `-ngl 99 --n-cpu-moe 44 -c 65536 -fa on -ctk q8_0 -ctv q8_0`.\n\nEight sequential chat completions, one `selected slot by LRU` switch observed in the log, no assert, all outputs correct, server still up afterwards. To be precise about scope: that is one slot switch, not a sustained hammering, but it is the reported failure point.\n\n@mjungnickel18 worth rebuilding from the current head before spending more time on it.\n\nAlso validated the rebase itself against a tuned baseline on the same box, no regression:\n\n```\n              af1ffaf37    072f519f6\ncode-edit       30.02        29.50\nprose           21.24        21.30\nprefill        138.0        138.0\n```\n\nA cross-file reasoning check still passes at the new head. Consumer sm_120 has been stable across roughly 45 server starts today, CUDA 13.1 toolkit matching a 13.1 driver.\n\nCould not help with the convert/quantize half. `llama-quantize` correctly refuses with `requantizing from type q8_0 is disabled`, so it needs the bf16 source and I do not have the disk for the 360GB. Looks like @ServeurpersoCom has that covered.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5443041531/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"resolved"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5443042618","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742#issuecomment-5443042618","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27742","id":5443042618,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABRG49Og","user":{"login":"mjungnickel18","id":41702029,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxNzAyMDI5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41702029?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjungnickel18","html_url":"https://github.com/mjungnickel18","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjungnickel18/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjungnickel18/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjungnickel18/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjungnickel18/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjungnickel18/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjungnickel18/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjungnickel18/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjungnickel18/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjungnickel18/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T17:50:36Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T17:50:36Z","body":"@ggerganov Thanks for clarifying. This is all changing so fast. Thank you for your incredible work!","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5443042618/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5443200834","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742#issuecomment-5443200834","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27742","id":5443200834,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABRHCnQg","user":{"login":"ggerganov","id":1991296,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTEyOTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1991296?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov","html_url":"https://github.com/ggerganov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T18:03:42Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T18:03:42Z","body":"We have a lot of graph inputs that are causing extra graph splits:\r\n\r\n```\r\nsched_reserve: graph nodes  = 7898\r\nsched_reserve: graph splits = 6\r\n...\r\n\r\nnode #3813 (       ADD):            node_3813 (  20M) [ MTL0         ] use=1,c=1:            node_3811 (  20M) [ MTL0         ]    (reshaped) (view) (  79M) [ MTL0         ]\r\nnode #3814 (     SCALE):          hc_mixed-23 (  20M) [ MTL0         ] use=5,c=1:            node_3813 (  20M) [ MTL0         ]\r\nnode #3815 (   MUL_MAT):            node_3815 (   1M) [ MTL0         ] use=1,c=1: blk.23.indexer.k_pro ( 640K) [ MTL0         ]          hc_mixed-23 (  20M) [ MTL0         ]\r\n\r\n## SPLIT #4: MTL0 # 30 inputs: [leaf_682 (  16K)] [leaf_692 (   1M)] [leaf_694 (   1M)] [leaf_697 ( 512M)] [leaf_698 (   1M)] [leaf_798 (  16K)] [leaf_808 (   1M)] [leaf_810 (   1M)] [leaf_813 ( 512M)] [leaf_814 (   1M)] [leaf_914 (  16K)] [leaf_924 (   1M)] [leaf_926 (   1M)] [leaf_929 ( 512M)] [leaf_930 (   1M)] [leaf_1030 (  16K)] [leaf_1040 (   1M)] [leaf_1042 (   1M)] [leaf_1045 ( 512M)] [leaf_1046 (   1M)] [leaf_1146 (  16K)] [leaf_1156 (   1M)] [leaf_1158 (   1M)] [leaf_1161 ( 512M)] [leaf_1162 (   1M)] [leaf_1262 (  16K)] [leaf_1272 (   1M)] [leaf_1274 (   1M)] [leaf_1277 ( 512M)] [leaf_1278 (   1M)] \r\nnode #3818 (  SET_ROWS): cache_idx_k_l23 (vie (  64M) [ MTL0         ] use=0,c=1: indexer_k_raw-23 (vi (   1M) [ MTL0         ]      MTL0#leaf_682#0 (  16K) [ NULL         ]      cache_idx_k_l23 (  64M) [ MTL0         ]\r\nnode #3819 (   MUL_MAT):         Qcur_full-23 (  96M) [ MTL0         ] use=2,c=1: blk.23.attn_q.weight (  31M) [ MTL0         ]          hc_mixed-23 (  20M) [ MTL0         ]\r\nnode #3821 (  RMS_NORM):              norm-23 (  48M) [ MTL0         ] use=1,c=1:     Qcur_reshaped-23 (  95M) [ MTL0         ]\r\n```\r\n\r\nWith https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/26625, these should be easier to spot and diagnose.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5443200834/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5443231723","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742#issuecomment-5443231723","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27742","id":5443231723,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABRHEf6w","user":{"login":"ngxson","id":7702203,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3MDIyMDM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7702203?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ngxson","html_url":"https://github.com/ngxson","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ngxson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ngxson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ngxson/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ngxson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ngxson/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ngxson/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ngxson/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ngxson/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ngxson/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T18:06:11Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T18:06:11Z","body":"> We have a lot of graph inputs that are causing extra graph splits:\r\n\r\nyes I'm pushing a fix for this too","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5443231723/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5443236760","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742#issuecomment-5443236760","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27742","id":5443236760,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABRHEzmA","user":{"login":"kyunghyunr","id":54661208,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0NjYxMjA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54661208?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyunghyunr","html_url":"https://github.com/kyunghyunr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyunghyunr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyunghyunr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyunghyunr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyunghyunr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyunghyunr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyunghyunr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyunghyunr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyunghyunr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyunghyunr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T18:06:35Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T18:07:18Z","body":"## qwen4exp: per-request host memory leak + context-proportional indexer buffer OOM\n\nRunning the unsloth GGUF on 3x RTX 3090 (72GB VRAM, 108GB RAM) with the latest PR head (6c5afc86), `UD-Q3_K_XL`, `-ts 15,16,17`, n-gram/PLE offloaded to CPU via `--override-tensor \"^per_layer_token_embd.weight$=CPU\"`, context 160K, `-ub 512`.\n\nTwo distinct issues observed after hours of use:\n\n### 1. Per-request host memory leak (~300 MB/request)\n\nSending **identical short requests** (`max_tokens=30..50`, `enable_thinking=false`, fresh conversation each) grows the process RSS monotonically with no plateau:\n\n- 5 requests: **+1.3 GB** (~260 MB/request)\n- 15 requests: **+4.8 GB** (~320 MB/request)\n\nThe context does not grow between these requests (each is a fresh tiny conversation), so this is not buffer growth — memory is leaked and never reclaimed. RSS does not drop when idle. The recent commit `fix the qwen4exp PLE history seq_rm(-1) iterator invalidation` (24ea62df) does **not** fix it (verified after rebuild).\n\n### 2. Context-proportional indexer buffer → cudaMalloc OOM\n\nDuring long-context use, the QSA indexer's expanded-score buffer grows with the **filled** context length and is requested per attention-GPU:\n\n- ~64K filled context: ~1.06 GB\n- ~105K filled context: ~1.45 GB\n\nThis exceeds the free VRAM on the tightest GPU (model weights leave only ~1.4 GB/GPU free at 160K ctx) and crashes the server:\n\n```\nallocating 1446.15 MiB on device 0: cudaMalloc failed: out of memory\nggml_gallocr_reserve_n_impl: failed to allocate CUDA0 buffer\n```\n\nWorkaround notes: `--no-kv-offload` avoids the VRAM pressure but drops decode speed 45 → 13-14 tok/s, so it is not viable. Reducing `-ub` does not shrink the dominating capacity-based component.\n\n### Setup\n- Build: unslothai/llama.cpp @ `qwen4exp/qwen3.8-flash-next` (6c5afc86) + local `graph_max_nodes` patch for `LLM_ARCH_QWEN4EXP` (later seen applied upstream)\n- CUDA 12.0, gcc-12, `-DGGML_CUDA=ON -DCMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES=86`\n- Model: unsloth/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GGUF UD-Q3_K_XL + mmproj-F16\n\nHappy to provide logs or run specific repro steps if useful.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5443236760/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"low-quality"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5443291819","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742#issuecomment-5443291819","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27742","id":5443291819,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABRHIKqw","user":{"login":"ggerganov","id":1991296,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTEyOTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1991296?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov","html_url":"https://github.com/ggerganov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T18:11:09Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T18:11:09Z","body":"> Converting here: https://github.com/ggml-org/convert/actions/runs/33095640791/job/98599706944\r\n\r\nConversion worked without issues: https://huggingface.co/ggml-org/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GGUF","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5443291819/reactions","total_count":12,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":8,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5443504973","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742#issuecomment-5443504973","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27742","id":5443504973,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABRHVLTQ","user":{"login":"sirfyyn","id":31549942,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNTQ5OTQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31549942?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sirfyyn","html_url":"https://github.com/sirfyyn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sirfyyn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sirfyyn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sirfyyn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sirfyyn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sirfyyn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sirfyyn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sirfyyn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sirfyyn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sirfyyn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T18:28:01Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T18:28:01Z","body":"Adjacent to the graph-inputs work above, in case it is useful while that code is open:\n**`qwen4exp` never reuses a graph, and one missing override is enough to explain it.**\n\nAt head `61b62d847`, `llm_graph_input_ple` is the architecture's only own graph input and it does\nnot override `can_reuse`. The base returns `false` by design:\n\n```cpp\n// llama-graph.h:113\nvirtual bool can_reuse(const llm_graph_params & params) {\n    // returning false here by default will prevent from reusing the graph if the check\n    //   for the input type has not been implemented yet\n    return false;\n}\n```\n\n`llama-context.cpp:1339` gates on `res->can_reuse(gparams)`, and PLE sits at `ple_layer_ids`, so it\nis present in every forward pass. The result is that the whole 49-layer graph is rebuilt per token.\n\n**Same engine, two architectures, from our logs:**\n\n| model | own `llm_graph_input_*` classes | `graphs reused` |\n|---|---|---|\n| `deepseek4` (DeepSeek-V4-Flash) | 0 — uses only the shared inputs, which all implement it | 37 · 70 · 77 |\n| `qwen4exp` (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next) | 1, no `can_reuse` | 0 · 0 · 0 |\n\n`deepseek4.cpp` and `dflash.cpp` declare no input classes of their own, so nothing can veto reuse\nthere. That is the only structural difference we could find between the two cases.\n\n**What the check would need.** The class holds a single tensor, `rows`, I32\n`[ple_n_heads * n_tokens]`, and `set_input` recomputes the hashed row indices on every call — so\nonly the shape has to match, not the contents:\n\n```cpp\nbool can_reuse(const llm_graph_params & params) override {\n    const auto & hp = pmodel.hparams;\n    return rows && rows->ne[0] == (int64_t) hp.ple_n_heads * params.ubatch.n_tokens;\n}\n```\n\nSince `61b62d847` also carries `mctx` (predecessor tokens live in the attention KV cells), that\npointer presumably needs refreshing from `params.mctx` the way `llm_graph_input_attn_kv::can_reuse`\ndoes — we have not run that variant.\n\n**What we have not measured: the cost.** We have the before/after contrast in `graphs reused`, and\nthe structural reason, but not a throughput delta — our own build has an extra input class of its\nown, so a local A/B would not isolate this cleanly. `LLAMA_GRAPH_REUSE_DISABLE` makes the\ncomparison possible on a build that has the override. We did not want to quote a number we had not\ntaken.\n\nHappy to test a patch on 2× RTX PRO Blackwell (CUDA 12.8, driver 610) if that is useful. Greedy\nequivalence at `temperature 0` with `LLAMA_GRAPH_REUSE_DISABLE=1` versus without would be the\ncheck we would run first — a false positive here changes output silently rather than crashing.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5443504973/reactions","total_count":6,"+1":1,"-1":4,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":1,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5443541708","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742#issuecomment-5443541708","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27742","id":5443541708,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABRHXazA","user":{"login":"Kononnable","id":9082099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwODIwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9082099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kononnable","html_url":"https://github.com/Kononnable","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kononnable/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kononnable/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kononnable/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kononnable/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kononnable/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kononnable/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kononnable/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kononnable/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kononnable/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T18:31:13Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T18:33:23Z","body":"I've got two different problems when trying to use it with rpc and `-ot`, that I didn't see reported yet.\r\n\r\n1) Changing load mode dio/mmap changes reported buffer sizes\r\n\r\nPC1: GPU(HIP), CPU\r\nPC2: RPC0(CPU)\r\n\r\nEmbeddings on local cpu, experts split by layer on both CPUs, attention and other tensors on local GPU\r\n`build/bin/llama-completion -lv 5 --fit off -c 7000 -m /models/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-UD-Q2_K_XL-00001-of-00003.gguf  -no-cnv -f ./prompt_1600.txt -n 1000  -sm layer --rpc 172.18.10.2:50052 -ot \"blk\\\\.[0-9]?[012345678]\\\\.ffn_(up|down|gate|gate_up)_(ch|)exps=RPC0[172.18.10.2:50052],.ffn_(up|down|gate|gate_up)_(ch|)exps=CPU,per_layer_token_embd=CPU\" -lm dio -ts 0,1`\r\ndio:\r\n```\r\n0.03.074.036 I load_tensors:          CPU model buffer size = 27465.95 MiB\r\n0.03.074.037 I load_tensors:        ROCm0 model buffer size =  3372.25 MiB\r\n0.03.074.038 I load_tensors:    ROCm_Host model buffer size =  4066.80 MiB\r\n0.03.074.039 I load_tensors: RPC0[172.18.10.2:50052] model buffer size = 40300.00 MiB\r\n```\r\nmmap:\r\n```\r\n0.08.174.783 I load_tensors:   CPU_Mapped model buffer size = 47310.62 MiB\r\n0.08.174.783 I load_tensors:   CPU_Mapped model buffer size = 19725.13 MiB\r\n0.08.174.784 I load_tensors:        ROCm0 model buffer size =  3372.25 MiB\r\n0.08.174.785 I load_tensors: RPC0[172.18.10.2:50052] model buffer size = 40300.00 MiB\r\n```\r\nmmap mode shows much higher numbers (75GB vs 110GB). Not sure if underneath mmap points to the same memory and this is just a visual/accounting problem or not.\r\n[dio.log](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/31527152/dio.log)\r\n[mmap.log](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/31527156/mmap.log)\r\n\r\n\r\n2) TOP_K failed\r\n\r\nHardware (client/server switched from previous test):\r\nPC1: CPU\r\nPC2: RPC0 (GPU, HIP), RPC1(CPU)\r\n\r\n\r\nEmbeddings on local cpu, experts split by layer on both CPUs, attention and other tensors on RPC0(GPU)\r\n\r\n`build/bin/llama-completion -lv 5 --fit off -c 7000 -m ~/models/models/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-UD-Q2_K_XL-00001-of-00003.gguf  -no-cnv -f ../prompt_1600.txt -n 1000  -sm layer --rpc 172.18.11.10:50052 -ot \"blk\\\\.[0-9]?[01234]\\\\.ffn_(up|down|gate|gate_up)_(ch|)exps=RPC1[172.18.11.10:50052],.ffn_(up|down|gate|gate_up)_(ch|)exps=CPU\" -lm dio -ts 1,0,0 2`\r\n\r\nDuring PP ggml-rpc-server throws:\r\n```\r\nggml_cuda_compute_forward: TOP_K failed\r\nROCm error: invalid configuration argument\r\n  current device: 0, in function ggml_cuda_compute_forward at /home/kononnable/repos/kononnable/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu:2412\r\n  err\r\n/home/kononnable/repos/kononnable/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu:107: ROCm error\r\n[New LWP 115497]\r\n```\r\nSame command passes for Qwen3-Coder-Next and Qwen 36B-A3B, so likely architecture related.\r\n\r\nReproduced on 072f519 (~1hr ago).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5443541708/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"off-topic"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5443579687","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742#issuecomment-5443579687","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27742","id":5443579687,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABRHZvJw","user":{"login":"ggerganov","id":1991296,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTEyOTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1991296?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov","html_url":"https://github.com/ggerganov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ggerganov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T18:34:19Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T18:34:19Z","body":"@sirfyyn You could just say: \"graph reuse does not work\" and it would be enough lol","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5443579687/reactions","total_count":28,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":28,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5443701121","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742#issuecomment-5443701121","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27742","id":5443701121,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABRHhJgQ","user":{"login":"kyunghyunr","id":54661208,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0NjYxMjA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54661208?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyunghyunr","html_url":"https://github.com/kyunghyunr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyunghyunr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyunghyunr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyunghyunr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyunghyunr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyunghyunr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyunghyunr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyunghyunr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyunghyunr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyunghyunr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T18:44:11Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T18:44:32Z","body":"Tested the `can_reuse` idea on 3x RTX 3090 (same box as the leak report above). Two findings:\n\n**1. `llm_graph_input_ple` alone is not the only blocker — `llm_graph_input_qsa` also lacks `can_reuse`.**\n\nAt head `61b62d847`, qwen4exp has TWO arch-local graph inputs in `src/models/qwen4exp.cpp`:\n- `llm_graph_input_qsa` (~line 417)\n- `llm_graph_input_ple` (~line 931)\n\nAdding only the PLE override kept `graphs reused = 0`. Adding both brought it into the hundreds.\n\nThe QSA override used:\n\n```cpp\nbool can_reuse(const llm_graph_params & params) override {\n    this->mctx = static_cast<const llama_memory_hybrid_idx_context *>(params.mctx);\n    if (!mctx || !mctx->get_idx()) return false;\n    const int64_t n_kv = (int64_t) mctx->get_idx()->get_n_kv();\n    const int64_t ns   = (int64_t) mctx->get_n_stream();\n    if (ns == 0) return false;\n    const int64_t n_blocks = n_kv / ratio;\n    const int64_t n_tps    = (int64_t) params.ubatch.n_tokens / ns;\n    bool res = true;\n    res &= k_idxs    && k_idxs->ne[0]    == (int64_t) params.ubatch.n_tokens;\n    res &= cell_blk  && cell_blk->ne[0]  == n_kv && cell_blk->ne[1] == ns;\n    res &= blk_cells && blk_cells->ne[0] == (int64_t) ratio * n_blocks && blk_cells->ne[1] == ns;\n    res &= blk_pos   && blk_pos->ne[0]   == 4 * n_blocks * ns;\n    res &= bias      && bias->ne[0]      == (blk_bias ? n_blocks : n_kv) && bias->ne[1] == n_tps && bias->ne[2] == ns;\n    return res;\n}\n```\n\n**2. Throughput delta (the number that was missing):**\n\n3x RTX 3090, UD-Q3_K_XL, instruct-mode decode, warmed:\n- before: ~45 tok/s, `graphs reused = 0`\n- after: **~57 tok/s (+25%)**, `graphs reused` climbs into the hundreds\n\n**3. Correctness spot-check:**\n\nGreedy (temp 0) same-session repeats are byte-identical with reuse enabled (the `graphs reused` counter increments across the repeats). Cross-session first-request outputs can differ slightly, but that reproduces with reuse disabled as well, so it looks like session-level non-determinism rather than the reuse path.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5443701121/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"low-quality"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5443877778","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742#issuecomment-5443877778","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27742","id":5443877778,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABRHr7kg","user":{"login":"ServeurpersoCom","id":4873680,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NzM2ODA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4873680?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom","html_url":"https://github.com/ServeurpersoCom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T18:59:51Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T18:59:51Z","body":"The llm_graph_input_ple reuse fix is a big win here","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5443877778/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":3,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":2,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5443897180","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742#issuecomment-5443897180","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27742","id":5443897180,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABRHtHXA","user":{"login":"ngxson","id":7702203,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3MDIyMDM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7702203?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ngxson","html_url":"https://github.com/ngxson","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ngxson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ngxson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ngxson/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ngxson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ngxson/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ngxson/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ngxson/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ngxson/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ngxson/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T19:01:28Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T19:01:54Z","body":"Let's merge this once the CI passes. Fixes and improvements should be follow-up PRs\r\n\r\n@danielhanchen feel free to push the MTP as a follow-up PR","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5443897180/reactions","total_count":43,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":18,"confused":0,"heart":10,"rocket":15,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5444042873","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742#issuecomment-5444042873","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27742","id":5444042873,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABRH2AeQ","user":{"login":"coeniebeyers","id":5429884,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0Mjk4ODQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5429884?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coeniebeyers","html_url":"https://github.com/coeniebeyers","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coeniebeyers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coeniebeyers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coeniebeyers/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coeniebeyers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coeniebeyers/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coeniebeyers/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coeniebeyers/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coeniebeyers/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coeniebeyers/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T19:13:10Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T19:13:10Z","body":"Eval bug: Vulkan push-constant size assertion in ggml_vk_topk (dispatching the sum_rows_f32 pipeline) — Qwen3.8-Flash-Next (qwen4exp) with Flash Attention on longer sequences\n\n### Name and Version\n\nversion: 0.3.0-dev (build 1, commit 6c5afc8), `qwen4exp` branch (PR #27742), built with `-DGGML_VULKAN=ON -DGGML_RPC=ON`.\n\nVulkan device (both machines): `AMD Radeon 780M Graphics (RADV PHOENIX)` — integrated GPU, `uma: 1`, fp16: 1.\n\n### Operating systems\n\nLinux (Ubuntu)\n\n### Which llama.cpp modules do you know to be affected?\n\nVulkan backend (ggml-vulkan), RPC (ggml-rpc)\n\n### Command line\n\nThe model is split across two machines with RPC; both run the Vulkan backend on a Radeon 780M.\n\nMachine B (RPC worker):\n```\nggml-rpc-server -H 0.0.0.0 -p 50052 -t 8\n```\n\nMachine A (client):\n```\nllama-server -m Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-UD-IQ1_S-00001-of-00003.gguf \\\n  --rpc <machineB>:50052 -ngl 99 -fa on -ctk q8_0 -ctv q8_0 \\\n  -c 8192 -b 512 -ub 128 --parallel 1 --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8090\n```\n\nModel: `unsloth/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GGUF` (reproduced on both UD-IQ1_S and UD-IQ4_XS).\n\n### Problem description & steps to reproduce\n\nWith Flash Attention on, generation runs correctly for a while and then the Vulkan worker aborts on this assertion once the sequence gets long enough (about 700 generated tokens in this run):\n\n```\nggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp:8172:\nGGML_ASSERT(pipeline->push_constant_size == push_constant_size(push_constants)) failed\n```\n\nI added a one-line print just before that assertion to see which pipeline and which sizes were involved:\n\n```\nPUSHCONST_MISMATCH pipeline=sum_rows_f32 expected=60 got=28\n```\n\nSo the `sum_rows_f32` pipeline — which is created with `push_constant_size = sizeof(vk_op_sum_rows_push_constants)` (60 bytes) — is being dispatched with a 28-byte push-constant block. 28 bytes is exactly `sizeof(vk_op_topk_push_constants)` (7 × uint32). Resolving the backtrace with addr2line points at the top-k code path:\n\n```\nggml_vk_topk(...)          ggml-vulkan.cpp\nggml_vk_build_graph(...)\nggml_backend_vk_graph_compute(...)\n```\n\nSo a top-k dispatch is ending up on the `sum_rows_f32` pipeline (or that pipeline is being handed the top-k push-constant struct). It only shows up with `-fa on` and only once the sequence is long enough, which fits Flash-Next selecting top-k positions in its sparse attention (that top-k grows with sequence length), and/or its 512-expert top-10 MoE routing. It's a size mismatch between a pipeline's declared push-constant block and the struct passed at dispatch, so it looks like a wrong-pipeline or wrong-struct pairing rather than anything hardware-related — the GPU has ~58 GB free and runs the model fine up to that point.\n\nFor comparison, **without** `-fa` it instead fails a little later (~800 tokens) with a device-buffer-size error (`ErrorOutOfDeviceMemory` / \"requested buffer size exceeds device buffer size limit\"), which looks like the known large-compute-buffer behaviour when Flash Attention is off. So on this Vulkan + RPC setup Flash-Next can't currently produce answers longer than roughly 700–800 tokens in either mode.\n\nSteps to make it happen:\n1. Build the `qwen4exp` branch with Vulkan and RPC enabled.\n2. Start `ggml-rpc-server` (Vulkan) on machine B.\n3. Start `llama-server` on machine A with `--rpc`, `-fa on`, `-ngl 99` (command above).\n4. Send a prompt that produces a long answer (more than ~700 tokens), for example: \"List the integers from 1 to 120 and, for each, print its square and cube on one line.\"\n5. The RPC worker aborts on the assertion; the client aborts right after because the worker is gone.\n\n### First Bad Commit\n\nNot bisected — `qwen4exp` is a feature branch. Observed on commit 6c5afc8.\n\n### Relevant log output\n\nRPC worker (machine B), with the extra `PUSHCONST_MISMATCH` print added before the assertion:\n```\nPUSHCONST_MISMATCH pipeline=sum_rows_f32 expected=60 got=28\nggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp:8172: GGML_ASSERT(pipeline->push_constant_size == push_constant_size(push_constants)) failed\nlibggml-base.so.0(ggml_abort+0x15b)\nlibggml-vulkan.so.0  ggml_vk_dispatch_pipeline<...>\nlibggml-vulkan.so.0  ggml_vk_topk(...)\nlibggml-vulkan.so.0  ggml_vk_build_graph(...)\nlibggml-vulkan.so.0  ggml_backend_vk_graph_compute(...)\nlibggml-rpc.so.0     rpc_server::graph_compute(...)\n```\n\nClient (machine A):\n```\nggml/src/ggml-rpc/ggml-rpc.cpp:522: Remote RPC server crashed or returned malformed response\nrecv failed (bytes_recv=0, size_to_recv=8)\n```\n\nHappy to grab full `--verbose` logs or test a patch.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5444042873/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5444894219","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742#issuecomment-5444894219","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27742","id":5444894219,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABRIp-Cw","user":{"login":"erazortt","id":4786333,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3ODYzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4786333?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/erazortt","html_url":"https://github.com/erazortt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erazortt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erazortt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erazortt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erazortt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erazortt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erazortt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erazortt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erazortt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erazortt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T20:33:51Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T20:35:41Z","body":"I tried converting the full model using the convert_hf_to_gguf.py but I am getting this error. What am I doing wrong?\r\n\r\n(I used the follwing command: python convert_hf_to_gguf.py --outtype bf16 /f/LLM/models/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next/)\r\n\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"D:\\sources\\llama.cpp\\convert_hf_to_gguf.py\", line 307, in <module>\r\n    main()\r\n  File \"D:\\sources\\llama.cpp\\convert_hf_to_gguf.py\", line 301, in main\r\n    model_instance.write()\r\n  File \"D:\\sources\\llama.cpp\\conversion\\base.py\", line 1073, in write\r\n    self.prepare_metadata(vocab_only=False)\r\n  File \"D:\\sources\\llama.cpp\\conversion\\qwen.py\", line 358, in prepare_metadata\r\n    super().prepare_metadata(vocab_only=vocab_only)  # ty: ignore[unresolved-attribute]\r\n    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\r\n  File \"D:\\sources\\llama.cpp\\conversion\\base.py\", line 1270, in prepare_metadata\r\n    self.set_vocab()\r\n  File \"D:\\sources\\llama.cpp\\conversion\\base.py\", line 1242, in set_vocab\r\n    self._set_vocab_gpt2()\r\n  File \"D:\\sources\\llama.cpp\\conversion\\base.py\", line 1791, in _set_vocab_gpt2\r\n    tokens, toktypes, tokpre = self.get_vocab_base()\r\n                               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\r\n  File \"D:\\sources\\llama.cpp\\conversion\\base.py\", line 1424, in get_vocab_base\r\n    tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(self.dir_model)\r\n                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\r\n  File \"D:\\sources\\llama.cpp\\.venv\\Lib\\site-packages\\transformers\\models\\auto\\tokenization_auto.py\", line 1156, in from_pretrained\r\n    return tokenizer_class.from_pretrained(pretrained_model_name_or_path, *inputs, **kwargs)\r\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\r\n  File \"D:\\sources\\llama.cpp\\.venv\\Lib\\site-packages\\transformers\\tokenization_utils_base.py\", line 2113, in from_pretrained\r\n    return cls._from_pretrained(\r\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\r\n  File \"D:\\sources\\llama.cpp\\.venv\\Lib\\site-packages\\transformers\\tokenization_utils_base.py\", line 2359, in _from_pretrained\r\n    tokenizer = cls(*init_inputs, **init_kwargs)\r\n                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\r\n  File \"D:\\sources\\llama.cpp\\.venv\\Lib\\site-packages\\transformers\\models\\qwen2\\tokenization_qwen2_fast.py\", line 120, in __init__\r\n    super().__init__(\r\n  File \"D:\\sources\\llama.cpp\\.venv\\Lib\\site-packages\\transformers\\tokenization_utils_fast.py\", line 117, in __init__\r\n    fast_tokenizer = TokenizerFast.from_file(fast_tokenizer_file)\r\n                     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\r\nException: expected value at line 1 column 1","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5444894219/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5444929277","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742#issuecomment-5444929277","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27742","id":5444929277,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABRIsG_Q","user":{"login":"ServeurpersoCom","id":4873680,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NzM2ODA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4873680?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom","html_url":"https://github.com/ServeurpersoCom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ServeurpersoCom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T20:37:17Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T20:38:40Z","body":"Look like your tokenizer.json is not JSON, can you check it and redownload it from the model page? (you cloned without git-lfs and only got the pointer file ?)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5444929277/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5444981077","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742#issuecomment-5444981077","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27742","id":5444981077,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABRIvRVQ","user":{"login":"erazortt","id":4786333,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3ODYzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4786333?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/erazortt","html_url":"https://github.com/erazortt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erazortt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erazortt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erazortt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erazortt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erazortt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erazortt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erazortt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erazortt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erazortt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T20:42:24Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T20:42:24Z","body":"crap, yes, thats exaclty what happened","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5444981077/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":3,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5446362556","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742#issuecomment-5446362556","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27742","id":5446362556,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABRKDlvA","user":{"login":"SamuelBerezhinskiy","id":64804168,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0ODA0MTY4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64804168?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamuelBerezhinskiy","html_url":"https://github.com/SamuelBerezhinskiy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamuelBerezhinskiy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamuelBerezhinskiy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamuelBerezhinskiy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamuelBerezhinskiy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamuelBerezhinskiy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamuelBerezhinskiy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamuelBerezhinskiy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamuelBerezhinskiy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamuelBerezhinskiy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T23:18:27Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T23:21:21Z","body":"> Eval bug: Vulkan push-constant size assertion in ggml_vk_topk (dispatching the sum_rows_f32 pipeline) — Qwen3.8-Flash-Next (qwen4exp) with Flash Attention on longer sequences\r\n> ### Name and Version\r\n> \r\n> version: 0.3.0-dev (build 1, commit [6c5afc8](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/6c5afc86ae84448ae4d744e357017e2c490ad9c3)), `qwen4exp` branch (PR #27742), built with `-DGGML_VULKAN=ON -DGGML_RPC=ON`.\r\n> \r\n> Vulkan device (both machines): `AMD Radeon 780M Graphics (RADV PHOENIX)` — integrated GPU, `uma: 1`, fp16: 1.\r\n> ### Operating systems\r\n> \r\n> Linux (Ubuntu)\r\n> ### Which llama.cpp modules do you know to be affected?\r\n> \r\n> Vulkan backend (ggml-vulkan), RPC (ggml-rpc)\r\n> ### Command line\r\n> \r\n> The model is split across two machines with RPC; both run the Vulkan backend on a Radeon 780M.\r\n> \r\n> Machine B (RPC worker):\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> ggml-rpc-server -H 0.0.0.0 -p 50052 -t 8\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> Machine A (client):\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> llama-server -m Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-UD-IQ1_S-00001-of-00003.gguf \\\r\n>   --rpc <machineB>:50052 -ngl 99 -fa on -ctk q8_0 -ctv q8_0 \\\r\n>   -c 8192 -b 512 -ub 128 --parallel 1 --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8090\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> Model: `unsloth/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GGUF` (reproduced on both UD-IQ1_S and UD-IQ4_XS).\r\n> ### Problem description & steps to reproduce\r\n> \r\n> With Flash Attention on, generation runs correctly for a while and then the Vulkan worker aborts on this assertion once the sequence gets long enough (about 700 generated tokens in this run):\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp:8172:\r\n> GGML_ASSERT(pipeline->push_constant_size == push_constant_size(push_constants)) failed\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> I added a one-line print just before that assertion to see which pipeline and which sizes were involved:\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> PUSHCONST_MISMATCH pipeline=sum_rows_f32 expected=60 got=28\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> So the `sum_rows_f32` pipeline — which is created with `push_constant_size = sizeof(vk_op_sum_rows_push_constants)` (60 bytes) — is being dispatched with a 28-byte push-constant block. 28 bytes is exactly `sizeof(vk_op_topk_push_constants)` (7 × uint32). Resolving the backtrace with addr2line points at the top-k code path:\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> ggml_vk_topk(...)          ggml-vulkan.cpp\r\n> ggml_vk_build_graph(...)\r\n> ggml_backend_vk_graph_compute(...)\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> So a top-k dispatch is ending up on the `sum_rows_f32` pipeline (or that pipeline is being handed the top-k push-constant struct). It only shows up with `-fa on` and only once the sequence is long enough, which fits Flash-Next selecting top-k positions in its sparse attention (that top-k grows with sequence length), and/or its 512-expert top-10 MoE routing. It's a size mismatch between a pipeline's declared push-constant block and the struct passed at dispatch, so it looks like a wrong-pipeline or wrong-struct pairing rather than anything hardware-related — the GPU has ~58 GB free and runs the model fine up to that point.\r\n> \r\n> For comparison, **without** `-fa` it instead fails a little later (~800 tokens) with a device-buffer-size error (`ErrorOutOfDeviceMemory` / \"requested buffer size exceeds device buffer size limit\"), which looks like the known large-compute-buffer behaviour when Flash Attention is off. So on this Vulkan + RPC setup Flash-Next can't currently produce answers longer than roughly 700–800 tokens in either mode.\r\n> \r\n> Steps to make it happen:\r\n> \r\n>     1. Build the `qwen4exp` branch with Vulkan and RPC enabled.\r\n> \r\n>     2. Start `ggml-rpc-server` (Vulkan) on machine B.\r\n> \r\n>     3. Start `llama-server` on machine A with `--rpc`, `-fa on`, `-ngl 99` (command above).\r\n> \r\n>     4. Send a prompt that produces a long answer (more than ~700 tokens), for example: \"List the integers from 1 to 120 and, for each, print its square and cube on one line.\"\r\n> \r\n>     5. The RPC worker aborts on the assertion; the client aborts right after because the worker is gone.\r\n> \r\n> \r\n> ### First Bad Commit\r\n> \r\n> Not bisected — `qwen4exp` is a feature branch. Observed on commit [6c5afc8](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/6c5afc86ae84448ae4d744e357017e2c490ad9c3).\r\n> ### Relevant log output\r\n> \r\n> RPC worker (machine B), with the extra `PUSHCONST_MISMATCH` print added before the assertion:\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> PUSHCONST_MISMATCH pipeline=sum_rows_f32 expected=60 got=28\r\n> ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp:8172: GGML_ASSERT(pipeline->push_constant_size == push_constant_size(push_constants)) failed\r\n> libggml-base.so.0(ggml_abort+0x15b)\r\n> libggml-vulkan.so.0  ggml_vk_dispatch_pipeline<...>\r\n> libggml-vulkan.so.0  ggml_vk_topk(...)\r\n> libggml-vulkan.so.0  ggml_vk_build_graph(...)\r\n> libggml-vulkan.so.0  ggml_backend_vk_graph_compute(...)\r\n> libggml-rpc.so.0     rpc_server::graph_compute(...)\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> Client (machine A):\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> ggml/src/ggml-rpc/ggml-rpc.cpp:522: Remote RPC server crashed or returned malformed response\r\n> recv failed (bytes_recv=0, size_to_recv=8)\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> Happy to grab full `--verbose` logs or test a patch.\r\n\r\n\r\nI ran into the same problem on a Vulkan, multi node system. The patch i used to keep moving:\r\n\r\n```c++\r\ndiff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-rpc/ggml-rpc.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-rpc/ggml-rpc.cpp\r\nindex 9aa5883..320c151 100644\r\n--- a/ggml/src/ggml-rpc/ggml-rpc.cpp\r\n+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-rpc/ggml-rpc.cpp\r\n@@ -2181,7 +2181,9 @@ static bool ggml_backend_rpc_device_supports_op(ggml_backend_dev_t dev, const st\r\n     GGML_UNUSED(dev);\r\n     GGML_UNUSED(op);\r\n     //TODO: call the remote backend and cache the results\r\n-    return true;\r\n+    // Remote backends run graphs without a supports_op gate, and the Vulkan topk\r\n+    // pipeline table only covers k < 1024, so keep large top-k nodes on a local backend.\r\n+    return !(op->op == GGML_OP_TOP_K && op->ne[0] >= 1024);\r\n }\r\n \r\n static bool ggml_backend_rpc_device_supports_buft(ggml_backend_dev_t dev, ggml_backend_buffer_type_t buft) {\r\ndiff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp\r\nindex 72e844a..59bc193 100644\r\n--- a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp\r\n+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp\r\n@@ -13906,6 +13906,13 @@ static void ggml_vk_topk(ggml_backend_vk_context * ctx, vk_context& subctx, cons\r\n     uint32_t nrows = ggml_nrows(src0);\r\n     uint32_t k = dst->ne[0];\r\n \r\n+    // ggml_vk_supports_op rejects k >= 1024, but the graph can still reach here\r\n+    // through backends that bypass that check (e.g. RPC). Fail loudly instead of\r\n+    // reading pipeline_topk_f32 out of bounds.\r\n+    if ((uint32_t) log2f(float(k)) + 1 >= num_topk_pipelines) {\r\n+        GGML_ABORT(\"ggml_vulkan: top_k with k = %u is not supported (k must be < 1024)\", k);\r\n+    }\r\n+\r\n     vk_op_topk_push_constants pc { ncols, ncols, ncols, k, nrows, 0, 0 };\r\n \r\n     if (ctx->prealloc_x_need_sync) {\r\n``` \r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5446362556/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5448204773","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742#issuecomment-5448204773","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27742","id":5448204773,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABRL0B5Q","user":{"login":"NightMustEnd","id":154791277,"node_id":"U_kgDOCTntbQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/154791277?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NightMustEnd","html_url":"https://github.com/NightMustEnd","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NightMustEnd/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NightMustEnd/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NightMustEnd/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NightMustEnd/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NightMustEnd/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NightMustEnd/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NightMustEnd/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NightMustEnd/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NightMustEnd/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-28T03:56:32Z","updated_at":"2026-08-28T03:56:32Z","body":"## Follow-up: intermittent citation-accuracy defect tied to slot reuse (not the crash bug)\n\nThanks for merging this — the slot-crossover crash fix (the indexer-cache restore logic in `llama-kv-cache.cpp` / `llama-memory-hybrid-idx.cpp`) is confirmed working in what actually landed at `6c84c7d5`. I diffed those files against the branch I originally tested (`pr-27742-tmp` @ `3d7baaebb`) and they're byte-identical, so this report applies to the merged code, not a stale fork.\n\n**What I tested:** `llama-server` with `Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-UD-Q3_K_XL` and `UD-IQ4_XS` (both Unsloth Dynamic quants), Vulkan backend, `-ngl 999 -fa on --reasoning-effort medium`, `--ctx-size 262144`. Ryzen AI Max+ 395 (gfx1151), 128GB UMA.\n\n**Crash fix — confirmed solid.** Default `n_slots=4`: 20 sequential requests + 5 rounds of 4 concurrent requests (40 total) with no crash, well past the old ~11-request threshold on the pre-fix build.\n\n**New defect — content accuracy degrades on slot reuse, not crash-inducing.** Task: a long synthetic document (64K–128K tokens) containing 3 mutually contradictory \"important record\" statements with specific dates, asking the model to find and quote the contradictions. Grading criterion: does the quoted date match the source exactly.\n\n| run | server state | slot | result |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| fresh boot, 1st request (64K) | empty | id 3 | correct quote |\n| fresh boot, 1st request (128K) | empty | id 3 | correct quote |\n| same server, 2nd request (128K, after a 64K request) | reused | id 2 | **misquoted digit** (2027→2026) |\n| soak test (40 reqs) then a fresh 64K request on the same server | reused | id 0 | **misquoted digit** |\n| `--parallel 1` (n_slots=1), 1st request (64K) | empty | id 0 | correct quote |\n| `--parallel 1`, 2nd request (128K, same server) | **reused id 0** | id 0 | **misquoted digit** |\n\nThe pattern holds across quant (Q3_K_XL and IQ4_XS both show it — ruled out quantization), context length (fails at 64K too once a slot has been reused — ruled out length-dependence), and slot count (`--parallel 1` still fails — ruled out \"just avoid multi-slot\"). The one thing that predicts failure in every run: whether the serving slot's cells were previously allocated-and-freed vs. genuinely fresh. Contradiction *detection* itself stays perfect (3/3) in every run — only the quoted digit inside an otherwise-correct answer drifts, which makes it look right at a glance and easy to miss in eval.\n\nGiven the crash fix in this PR is specifically about keeping the indexer cache's cell layout in sync with the attention cache's across slot restores, I suspect this is a related-but-distinct case: something in the QSA top-k selection path picking up stale cell state left over in a reused slot even when the restore path itself completes without asserting. I don't have a minimal repro at the ggml-graph level yet — happy to help narrow it down if useful, but wanted to flag it since it's a silent-wrong-answer failure mode rather than a crash, which is easy to miss in casual testing.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5448204773/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5450256471","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742#issuecomment-5450256471","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27742","id":5450256471,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABRNxQVw","user":{"login":"GlidLov","id":23376078,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzc2MDc4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23376078?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlidLov","html_url":"https://github.com/GlidLov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlidLov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlidLov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlidLov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlidLov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlidLov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlidLov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlidLov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlidLov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlidLov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-28T08:28:45Z","updated_at":"2026-08-28T08:28:45Z","body":"## Benchmarks on consumer GPUs, and why decode is bound by RAM latency\n\nThanks for this PR. I ran a fairly wide sweep on RTX 3090 and want to share numbers plus a few findings that might be actionable — including one that surprised me: **a dual-channel laptop delivers 2–3× the useful memory bandwidth of an 8-channel server** for this workload.\n\n**Setup:** `unsloth/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GGUF` `UD-Q4_K_XL` (111.3 GB, 4 shards), CUDA 12.8, `-DCMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES=86`, cloud instances (so expect variance from shared tenancy).\n\n### Results\n\n**1× RTX 3090 (24 GB)**\n\n| flags | ctx | prefill | decode | VRAM |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `-cmoe` | 8k | 34.5 t/s | 23.9 t/s | **7.3 GB** |\n| `-ncmoe 38` + `-ot \"per_layer_token_embd\\.weight=CPU\"` | 8k | 38.5 t/s | 25.9 t/s | 21.8 GB |\n| `-ncmoe 42` + `-ot ...` | 120k | 97.2 t/s | 13.9 t/s | 21.0 GB |\n| `-cmoe -b 2048 -ub 2048` | 245k | 77.2 t/s | 9.3 t/s | 21.6 GB |\n\n**2× RTX 3090 (48 GB)**\n\n| flags | ctx | prefill | decode | VRAM |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `-ncmoe 24 -ts 2.7,1` + `-ot ...` | 8k | 50.6 t/s | 31.8 t/s | 22.8 + 20.7 GB |\n| `-ncmoe 28 -ts 3.4,1` + `-ot ...` | 40k | 184.4 t/s | 22.7 t/s | 22.0 + 18.5 GB |\n\nNeedle-in-a-haystack retrieval was correct at every context length including 245k.\n\n### Finding 1 — passing `-ot \"per_layer_token_embd\\.weight=CPU\"` alongside `-cmoe` wastes ~11 GB of VRAM\n\nSame machine, same context, same prompt:\n\n| flags | prefill | decode | VRAM |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `-cmoe -ot \"per_layer_token_embd\\.weight=CPU\"` | 34.5 t/s | 23.3 t/s | 18.7 GB |\n| `-cmoe` alone | 34.5 t/s | 23.9 t/s | **7.3 GB** |\n\n`-cmoe` already places the PLE table correctly. Adding the explicit override costs 11.4 GB with no throughput benefit. Worth calling out in the docs — 7.3 GB means a 12 GB card can serve this model.\n\n### Finding 2 — `-ncmoe N` badly unbalances multi-GPU\n\n`-ncmoe N` removes experts from the **first** N layers. With the default layer split those land on GPU0, so GPU1 receives all the expert-heavy layers. On 2× 3090 with `-ncmoe 24` the allocator tried to place **37.8 GB on a single 24 GB device**:\n\n```\nggml_backend_cuda_buffer_type_alloc_buffer: allocating 37778.71 MiB on device 1: cudaMalloc failed: out of memory\n-alloc_tensor_range: failed to allocate CUDA1 buffer of size 39613846784\n```\n\nManual `-ts` compensation fixes it (`-ts 2.7,1` for `-ncmoe 24`), but the ratio has to be computed by hand from the expert-tensor sizes. Auto-balancing that split, or interleaving the CPU-offloaded layers instead of taking the first N, would make multi-GPU work out of the box.\n\n### Finding 3 — the CPU MoE threading work does not move decode\n\nTwo commits, **same machine, same model, same flags** (`-cmoe -c 8192 -b 4096 -ub 4096 -fa on --numa distribute`), EPYC 7742:\n\n| commit | active cores | decode (t=16) | decode (t=32) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `6c5afc86a` | 1 | 12.8 t/s | 11.8 t/s |\n| `072f519f6` | 31 | 12.7 t/s | 11.7 t/s |\n\n1 active core → 31, decode unchanged. So CPU compute is not the constraint.\n\nNor is sequential bandwidth. Active experts are ~1.03 GB/token at Q4; at 12.8 t/s that is **13.2 GB/s** of traffic, against ~200 GB/s of 8-channel DDR4 sequential capability.\n\n### Finding 4 — what actually bounds it: random-access bandwidth, and a laptop beats a server at it\n\nMoE gathers 10 of 512 experts per token at random — scattered reads across a ~100 GB working set, which is a latency problem, not a throughput one. I measured that pattern directly (random 1 MB blocks over a 48 GB buffer, touching every cache line):\n\n| threads | **EPYC 7742** — 8ch DDR4, 8 NUMA nodes | **i9-13980HX** — 2ch DDR5, 1 NUMA node |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 16.9 GB/s | 20.2 GB/s |\n| 8 | 23.3 GB/s | 55.9 GB/s |\n| 16 | 23.4 GB/s | 64.3 GB/s |\n| 24–32 | 33.7 GB/s | **67.0 GB/s** |\n\nA **mobile dual-channel part outperforms an 8-channel EPYC by ~3× at 16 threads.** The result held from an 8 GB to a 40 GB working set (55–61 GB/s), so it is not a TLB or cache artifact.\n\nWorth noting what the laptop was running: 2× 32 GB Crucial SO-DIMMs rated 5600 but **configured at DDR5-4800**. So 67 GB/s is what a modest, already-derated dual-channel setup achieves — not a tuned best case.\n\nTwo consequences:\n\n- Random-access bandwidth **saturates around 8 threads** on both platforms. That is exactly why going from 1 to 31 active cores changed nothing.\n- Channel count buys sequential throughput this workload never uses. What it costs is NUMA distance, and NUMA-remote random reads are latency-bound.\n\nMeasured decode tracks this metric across machines: 23 GB/s random → 12.8 t/s; a Zen 3 EPYC running the same config at 23.9 t/s implies ~45 GB/s. Both land near **57% of the random-access ceiling**.\n\n### Conclusion — RAM latency is the design constraint, and how to configure for it\n\nIf decode is bounded by random-access latency rather than compute or sequential bandwidth, the hardware advice inverts from the usual \"big server\" intuition:\n\n**1. Prefer single-NUMA over many memory channels.** A desktop or mobile platform with 2 channels and one NUMA node beat an 8-channel, 8-node server by 3×. Channels do not help scattered reads.\n\n**2. If you are on a server, set NPS1 in BIOS.** Many EPYC/Xeon boards default to NPS4 or NPS8. Under `-cmoe` the expert table is spread across all nodes and every gather has a high chance of landing remote. `--numa distribute` and `--numa isolate` measured within noise of each other (12.6 vs 12.3 t/s), so llama.cpp's NUMA flags do not compensate for a bad firmware topology.\n\n**3. Memory clock and timings matter more than capacity headroom.** Random-access bandwidth scales with latency, so faster/tighter DIMMs pay off directly.\n\n**4. Capacity forces derated memory speeds — but that matters less than you would think.** `-cmoe` needs ~100 GB resident for `UD-Q4_K_XL`, so 128 GB is the practical floor, and there is no way to reach it without derating: 4 DIMMs drop to ~3600 MT/s per JEDEC, and 64 GB modules are dual-rank, which costs speed too (LGA1851 falls to DDR5-4400 with dual-rank at 2 DIMMs per channel). The reassuring part is that the 67 GB/s figure above was measured at **DDR5-4800**, i.e. already in that derated range. Prefer 2 DIMMs over 4 where capacity allows, but do not pay a large premium chasing rated speed.\n\n**5. Threads: ~8 is enough.** Past that the memory subsystem saturates. On the EPYC, `-t 16` beat `-t 32` consistently (12.8 vs 11.8).\n\nIf it is useful, the optimization with headroom here looks like **expert prefetch / access-pattern work** — overlapping the gather with compute, or improving expert locality — rather than further threading. Happy to test a patch.\n\n### Smaller notes\n\n- `-b 4096 -ub 4096` needs a ~10.7 GB compute buffer at 250k ctx, which OOMs on 24 GB. `-b 2048 -ub 2048` fits (21.6 GB peak) and still lifts prefill from 61 → 77 t/s versus the default batch.\n- `-ctk q8_0 -ctv q8_0` was not needed to reach 245k on 24 GB — f16 KV fits, since only 12 of 48 layers carry a KV cache (~24 KB/token).\n- No disk I/O during decode with mmap (`read_bytes` stayed at 0, model in page cache); `--no-mmap` measured slower (10.6 vs 12.3 t/s).\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5450256471/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5452044018","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742#issuecomment-5452044018","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27742","id":5452044018,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABRPeW8g","user":{"login":"drew913s","id":227412309,"node_id":"U_kgDODY4JVQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/227412309?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/drew913s","html_url":"https://github.com/drew913s","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drew913s/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drew913s/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drew913s/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drew913s/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drew913s/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drew913s/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drew913s/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drew913s/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drew913s/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-28T11:37:06Z","updated_at":"2026-08-28T11:38:04Z","body":"Reporting a GB10-specific hang when loading this model with high -ngl values. Posting here since it's arch-specific to the model added in this PR.\n\n**Hardware:** DGX Spark GB10, 121 GiB unified memory (127 GB reported by /proc/meminfo).\n**Driver:** NVIDIA 580.173.02, CUDA 13.0, kernel 6.17.0-1029-nvidia (aarch64, Ubuntu 24.04).\n**Build:** b10692-ef6876693 (built from source on the box).\n**Model:** Qwen3.8-Flash-Next UD-Q4_K_XL (4 shards, ~104 GB on disk).\n\n## Symptom\n\nWith `-ngl` at or above ~45, `llama-cli` / `llama-server` spin forever inside `load_all_data` during model load and never return. The process does not crash, does not log an error — it just wedges. Sending SIGINT eventually produces a GDB backtrace from `ggml_uncaught_exception` but the relevant frame is inside `cudaMemcpyAsync → cuMemcpyHtoDAsync_v2 → ioctl`. Wall-clock: 180–190 s before I killed the processes in the bisect; they would not have self-terminated.\n\nThe `--no-mmap` variant hard-crashes at ~112 GB (`CUDA error: driver shutting down`, backtrace inside `ggml_backend_cuda_set_tensor_async`; dmesg shows `NVRM: NV_ERR_NO_MEMORY` at that point).\n\n## Bisect table\n\n| Config | -ngl | mmap | Result | Peak GPU MB | Peak sys cached MB |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| CPU only | 0 | mmap | OK, 3.5 t/s | 0 | ~8k used |\n| partial GPU | 10 | mmap | OK (load ~100 s) | ~34k | ~92k |\n| partial GPU | 30 | mmap | OK (load ~150 s), 4.9 t/s greedy | ~55k | ~71k |\n| partial GPU | 45 | mmap | **DEADLOCK** (never completes) | plateaus ~77k at 90 s | ~47k |\n| partial GPU | 62 | mmap | **DEADLOCK** (never completes) | plateaus ~84k at ~110 s | ~40k |\n| full offload | 99 | mmap | **DEADLOCK** | same plateau pattern | — |\n| full offload | 99 | no-mmap | **CRASH** at ~112 GB | ~112k then driver crash | 0 |\n\nThe monitor shows GPU (unified) usage growing steadily until ~77–84 GB then freezing. The sys cached column (kernel page cache — the mmap'd GGUF shards) simultaneously stops shrinking when GPU growth halts. This pattern — GPU plateau + page cache plateau + H2D ioctl block — points to the driver failing to allocate the next region and blocking inside the ioctl rather than returning an error.\n\n## Backtraces\n\n**ngl=45 (deadlock), stack at time of kill (gdb, ptrace_scope prevented full attach to blocked thread):**\n```\n#0  __futex_abstimed_wait_common64\n    [→ cli_server::wait_ready → cli_context::init → llama_cli]\n```\nThe model-load thread was blocked in `wait_ready`; the CUDA thread was inside `cudaMemcpyAsync` at the ioctl level (inferred from monotone GPU plateau with zero CPU activity after the freeze point).\n\n**ngl=99, --no-mmap (crash), saved from core:**\n```\nCUDA error: driver shutting down\n  in ggml_backend_cuda_set_tensor_async at ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu:2441\n  cudaMemcpyAsync((char*)tensor->data + offset, data, size, cudaMemcpyHostToDevice, stream)\n[backtrace exits through __cxa_finalize / signal_handler(SIGINT) / libcublasLt dtor]\n```\n\n## Notes\n\n- Partial offload at -ngl 10 or 30 is slower than CPU-only (3.5 t/s CPU vs ~4 t/s at -ngl 30) due to activation ping-pong; the useful range on GB10 would be full offload, which currently deadlocks.\n- The model itself is coherent on this hardware: -ngl 30 with mmap loads and generates correctly.\n\n## Request\n\nFail-fast at allocation rather than blocking indefinitely inside the ioctl. If the driver returns `NV_ERR_NO_MEMORY` (or `cudaErrorMemoryAllocation`) during `load_all_data`, surface it immediately with bytes requested and total already mapped, so the user can dial down -ngl to a working value. Currently there is no error message at all — the process hangs until killed.\n\nHappy to run additional diagnostics (specific tensor names at failure point, `nvidia-smi -q` output, different gdb approach) if useful.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5452044018/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5452546737","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742#issuecomment-5452546737","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27742","id":5452546737,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABRP9CsQ","user":{"login":"sjvrensburg","id":24384420,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0Mzg0NDIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24384420?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sjvrensburg","html_url":"https://github.com/sjvrensburg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sjvrensburg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sjvrensburg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sjvrensburg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sjvrensburg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sjvrensburg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sjvrensburg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sjvrensburg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sjvrensburg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sjvrensburg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-28T12:32:51Z","updated_at":"2026-08-28T12:32:51Z","body":"Data point on the `sum_rows_f32` / `ggml_vk_topk` push-constant assert reported above by @coeniebeyers: **it does not reproduce single-node**, which I think corroborates @SamuelBerezhinskiy's RPC diagnosis rather than adding a new case.\n\nSetup: `AMD Radeon 8060S (RADV STRIX_HALO)`, gfx1151, 128 GB unified, single machine, **no RPC**. Merged master `ca3d5a3e1` (b10665), `-DGGML_VULKAN=ON`. `unsloth/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GGUF` `UD-IQ3_XXS`, `-ngl 99 -fit off -lm dio -c 32768 --parallel 1 --jinja`, unquantized KV.\n\nBoth halves of the original report are clean here:\n\n| arm | result |\n|---|---|\n| `-fa on`, long generation | 2000 tokens, then 2728 tokens, `finish_reason: stop` — no assert |\n| `-fa off`, the reporter's own prompt (\"List the integers from 1 to 120 and, for each, print its square and cube on one line\") | 1906 tokens, completed through 120, `finish_reason: stop` — no `ErrorOutOfDeviceMemory` |\n\nZero `GGML_ASSERT` / `abort` / `DeviceLost` / buffer-size lines in either server log. Both runs went well past the ~700 and ~800 token thresholds in the report.\n\nThat matches the mechanism in @SamuelBerezhinskiy's patch: `ggml_vk_supports_op` already rejects `k >= 1024`, so single-node the large top-k node never reaches the Vulkan pipeline table; only `ggml_backend_rpc_device_supports_op`'s unconditional `return true` lets it through. So the bug looks **RPC-gated rather than Vulkan-gated**, and the `GGML_ABORT` half of that patch (failing loudly instead of indexing `pipeline_topk_f32` out of bounds) seems worth having regardless of how the routing is fixed.\n\nFlagging it mainly because the symptom as written — \"Vulkan + qwen4exp can't produce answers longer than ~700 tokens\" — reads as a general Vulkan incompatibility, and I expect that will draw duplicate reports from single-node Vulkan users who won't hit it. On this hardware the arch is fine.\n\nUnrelated but same hardware, in case anyone else lands here from it: #27797 (multi-segment prompts degrading to `//////` on gfx1151) is a **ROCm** report and does not reproduce on Vulkan either — system+user, three-segment multi-turn, and preamble+question all return coherent output.\n\nHappy to test patches on gfx1151/RADV.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5452546737/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5453872338","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742#issuecomment-5453872338","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27742","id":5453872338,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABRRN80g","user":{"login":"lviobio","id":76779534,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2Nzc5NTM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/76779534?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lviobio","html_url":"https://github.com/lviobio","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lviobio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lviobio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lviobio/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lviobio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lviobio/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lviobio/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lviobio/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lviobio/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lviobio/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-28T14:38:26Z","updated_at":"2026-08-28T14:38:26Z","body":"@danielhanchen Slot save/restore is accepted for `qwen4exp` but the restored state is never reused: the next request re-prefills the whole prompt. Same request path works on a non-hybrid arch, so this looks specific to the hybrid memory this PR introduces.\r\n\r\n**Build** `0.3.0-dev (build 10666, commit 4e97ac86e)`, Vulkan backend (RADV, AMD iGPU), Linux.\r\n**Model** `Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-UD-IQ4_XS` (3 shards).\r\n**Server** `llama-server -ngl 99 -fa on --ctx-size 65536 -np 1 --cache-type-k q8_0 --cache-type-v q8_0 --slot-save-path /kvcache/`\r\n\r\n### Reproduction\r\n\r\n```\r\nPOST /completion            {\"prompt\": P, \"n_predict\": 1, \"id_slot\": 0, \"cache_prompt\": true}\r\nPOST /slots/0?action=save   {\"filename\": \"probe.bin\"}\r\nPOST /slots/0?action=erase\r\nPOST /slots/0?action=restore {\"filename\": \"probe.bin\"}\r\nPOST /completion            {\"prompt\": P, \"n_predict\": 1, \"id_slot\": 0, \"cache_prompt\": true}   # same P\r\n```\r\n\r\n`timings.prompt_n` of the second completion, i.e. how many tokens had to be re-evaluated:\r\n\r\n| prompt | qwen4exp (this PR) | qwen35moe (control) |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| 57 tokens | 57 -> **57** (0% reused) | 57 -> **4** (93%) |\r\n| 2172 tokens | 2172 -> **2172** (0%) | 2172 -> **516** (76%) |\r\n| 16048 tokens | 16048 -> **16048** (0%) | — |\r\n\r\nThe control is `Qwen3.6-35B-A3B` (`general.architecture = qwen35moe`) on the same binary, same flags, same script, so the endpoint sequence itself is fine.\r\n\r\n`erase` reports the right `n_erased`, `restore` reports the right `n_restored` and a plausible `n_read`, and nothing is logged at any verbosity: the server simply re-prefills. On `qwen4exp` the token count after restore equals the cold count exactly, at every size.\r\n\r\n### Ruled out\r\n\r\n- **Prompt size** — 57, 2172 and 16048 tokens all give exactly 0% reuse.\r\n- **KV type** — `q8_0` and `f16`. The saved file changes size (119 -> 120 MB and 157 -> 192 MB for the two prompts), so the setting takes effect; behaviour does not change.\r\n- **Flash attention** — `-fa on` and `-fa off`.\r\n- **Prefix matching itself** — sending the same prompt twice *without* the erase/restore round trip reuses normally (57 -> 4). Only the disk round trip loses the state.\r\n\r\n### What the file size suggests\r\n\r\nSaved-state size against token count, `q8_0`:\r\n\r\n| tokens | file |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| 57 | 119.5 MB |\r\n| 361 | 124.5 MB |\r\n| 2701 | 166.7 MB |\r\n| 8101 | 263.9 MB |\r\n\r\nThat is **~118 MB independent of length plus ~17.6 KB/token**. The constant part is far larger than the per-token part for any realistic session, and it matches the fixed-size, per-sequence state this architecture adds (the gated delta-net recurrent state, and/or the QSA cache at budget 2048) rather than anything proportional to context.\r\n\r\nSo the fixed-size state does appear to be written. The question is whether it is read back and whether the server then treats the restored sequence as a usable prefix.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5453872338/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5456318533","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742#issuecomment-5456318533","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27742","id":5456318533,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABRTjQRQ","user":{"login":"anthonykim3197","id":203079572,"node_id":"U_kgDODBq_lA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203079572?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonykim3197","html_url":"https://github.com/anthonykim3197","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonykim3197/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonykim3197/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonykim3197/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonykim3197/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonykim3197/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonykim3197/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonykim3197/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonykim3197/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonykim3197/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-28T18:35:09Z","updated_at":"2026-08-28T18:35:09Z","body":"Heads-up for the qwen4exp authors: running this model at its full native context (`n_ctx 262144`) aborts with `CUDA error: invalid argument` — not OOM, VRAM sits at 68%.\n\nRoot cause is in core `ggml-cuda/norm.cu`, not in this PR: `rms_norm_f32` launches with `dim3 blocks_num(nrows, nchannels, nsamples)` and here `nchannels = n_ctx / 4` (hyper-connection count 4), so at 262,144 that is 65,536 — one past CUDA's `gridDim.y` limit. `binbcast.cu:317` already guards this case; `norm.cu` does not.\n\nPractical ceiling is `n_ctx 261,888` (99.9% of native), so impact is small, but the advertised 262,144 is unreachable.\n\nFiled with full reproduction, the instrumented launch log, and a 9/9 boundary model: #27901","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5456318533/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5458164455","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742#issuecomment-5458164455","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27742","id":5458164455,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABRVT65w","user":{"login":"MCFBMCFB","id":196979706,"node_id":"U_kgDOC72r-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/196979706?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MCFBMCFB","html_url":"https://github.com/MCFBMCFB","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MCFBMCFB/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MCFBMCFB/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MCFBMCFB/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MCFBMCFB/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MCFBMCFB/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MCFBMCFB/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MCFBMCFB/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MCFBMCFB/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MCFBMCFB/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-28T21:55:12Z","updated_at":"2026-08-28T21:55:12Z","body":"Testing this branch on 2× AMD Radeon AI PRO R9700 (gfx1201) under ROCm with the Unsloth `UD-Q4_K_XL` GGUF. It builds, loads and generates, but I hit two aborts that look architecture-specific. Reporting both with the control runs that isolate them.\r\n\r\n**Environment**\r\n\r\n- Build: `035e22731` (b10656), branch `pr-27742`\r\n- 2× AMD Radeon AI PRO R9700, gfx1201, 32 GiB each (device 0 PCIe Gen4 x16, device 1 Gen3 x4)\r\n- Ryzen 5 5600X (6C/12T), 78 GiB RAM, Ubuntu 24.04, ROCm/HIP backend\r\n- Model: `unsloth/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GGUF`, `UD-Q4_K_XL`, 4 shards, 103.68 GiB\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### 1. Build: PIE link failure on HIP\r\n\r\nThe default HIP configure fails at the final link step:\r\n\r\n```\r\n/usr/bin/ld: ../../ggml/src/ggml-hip/libggml-hip.a(ggml-cuda.cu.o): relocation R_X86_64_32 against `.rodata.str1.1' can not be used when making a PIE object; recompile with -fPIE\r\n```\r\n\r\nAdding `-DCMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE=ON` fixes it:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\ncmake -B build -DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF -DGGML_HIP=ON -DAMDGPU_TARGETS=gfx1201 \\\r\n      -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DCMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE=ON\r\n```\r\n\r\nNoting it here in case it is worth a line in the build docs for HIP; not necessarily something this PR needs to change.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### 2. Abort in `build_attn_qsa` with a quantised KV cache\r\n\r\nWith `-ctk q8_0 -ctv q8_0`, the model aborts during the warmup decode, before the server starts listening:\r\n\r\n```\r\n/home/michael/llama.cpp-qwen4exp/src/models/qwen4exp.cpp:544: GGML_ASSERT(inp->self_k_rot == nullptr && inp->self_v_rot == nullptr) failed\r\n```\r\n\r\n```\r\n#3  llama_model_qwen4exp::graph::build_attn_qsa(llm_graph_input_attn_kv*, ggml_tensor*, ggml_tensor*, ggml_tensor*, ggml_tensor*, float, int)\r\n#4  llama_model_qwen4exp::graph::build_layer_attn(llm_graph_input_attn_kv*, llama_memory_hybrid_idx_context const*, ggml_tensor*, ggml_tensor*, int*, int)\r\n#5  llama_model_qwen4exp::graph::graph(llama_model const&, llm_graph_params const&)\r\n#6  llama_model_qwen4exp::build_arch_graph(llm_graph_params const&) const\r\n#7  llama_model::build_graph(llm_graph_params const&) const\r\n#8  llama_context::process_ubatch(...)\r\n#9  llama_context::decode(llama_batch const&)\r\n```\r\n\r\nCommand:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nllama-server -m .../Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-UD-Q4_K_XL-00001-of-00004.gguf \\\r\n  --jinja -fa on -c 8192 -np 1 -ngl 999 --fit off \\\r\n  --tensor-split 1,1 -sm layer --main-gpu 1 -ncmoe 30 \\\r\n  -ctk q8_0 -ctv q8_0 --port 8090\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe same command without `-ctk/-ctv` loads and generates correctly. I did not separate `-ctk/-ctv q8_0` from `--fit off` in a controlled run, so quantised KV is the likely trigger rather than a confirmed one — but it matches other reports that this architecture needs f16 KV and that q8_0 on QSA misbehaves. Setting `LLAMA_ATTN_ROT_DISABLE=1` also avoids the assert, at a large throughput cost.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### 3. Abort in `llama_meta_device_get_split_state` with `-sm tensor`\r\n\r\n`-sm tensor` aborts during `load_tensors`:\r\n\r\n```\r\n/home/michael/llama.cpp-qwen4exp/src/llama-model.cpp:635: GGML_ASSERT(tensor->ne[axis] == n_embd + 2*n_embd_gqa) failed\r\n```\r\n\r\n```\r\n#3  llama_meta_device_get_split_state(ggml_tensor const*, void*)::{lambda(int, unsigned int)#1}::operator()(int, unsigned int) const\r\n#4  llama_meta_device_get_split_state(ggml_tensor const*, void*)\r\n#5  ggml_backend_meta_get_split_state(...)\r\n#7  ggml_backend_meta_buffer_init_tensor_impl(...)\r\n#8  ggml_backend_meta_alloc_ctx_tensors_from_buft()\r\n#9  llama_model_base::load_tensors(llama_model_loader&)\r\n```\r\n\r\n`blk.0.attn_qkv.weight` in this GGUF has shape `[2560, 10240]`. The assertion expects `n_embd + 2*n_embd_gqa` = 2560 + 2×512 = 3584. The tensor matches `pattern_qkv_weight` (`blk\\.\\d*\\.attn_qkv.weight`) but does not have the fused-QKV layout the split logic assumes; the 4× factor lines up with `qwen4exp.hyper_connection.count = 4` from the model metadata.\r\n\r\n**Control:** the same binary runs `-sm tensor` fine on a standard architecture on the same two GPUs, so tensor split itself works here:\r\n\r\n```\r\n| qwen35 27B Q8_0 | 32.89 GiB | 26.90 B | ROCm | 999 | tensor | 1 | pp512 | 307.73 ± 2.76 |\r\n| qwen35 27B Q8_0 | 32.89 GiB | 26.90 B | ROCm | 999 | tensor | 1 | tg128 |  20.62 ± 0.10 |\r\n```\r\n\r\nLines 594/603/661 in the same function already special-case SSM conv1d and gated-attention layouts, so qwen4exp may fit alongside those rather than needing new machinery.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Working configuration and numbers\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nllama-server -m .../Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-UD-Q4_K_XL-00001-of-00004.gguf \\\r\n  --jinja -fa on -c 8192 -np 1 -ngl 999 -sm layer --main-gpu 1 -ncmoe 30 --port 8090\r\n```\r\n\r\n`llama-bench`, same flags, `-r 3`:\r\n\r\n```\r\n| qwen4exp A3B Q4_K - Medium | 103.68 GiB | 176.94 B | ROCm | 999 | 30 | 1 | 1 | pp512 | 30.03 ± 3.98 |\r\n| qwen4exp A3B Q4_K - Medium | 103.68 GiB | 176.94 B | ROCm | 999 | 30 | 1 | 1 | tg128 |  9.15 ± 0.27 |\r\n```\r\n\r\nOutput is coherent. `graphs reused = 0` in every run, if that is unexpected.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Note on dual-GPU utilisation\r\n\r\nWith `-ncmoe`, only one GPU does meaningful compute. Reserved compute buffers are `ROCm0 1051.50 MiB` / `ROCm1 123.75 MiB`, identical under `--main-gpu 0` and `--main-gpu 1`.\r\n\r\nThis is the `!model.has_tensor_overrides()` condition in `llama-context.cpp:432` — `-ncmoe` registers tensor overrides, so pipeline parallelism is never enabled. The same binary prints `pipeline parallelism enabled` for the 27B without `-ncmoe`. Combined with issue 3 above, both multi-GPU concurrency paths are unavailable for this model: pipeline parallelism is disabled by the offload flag it needs in order to fit at all, and tensor parallelism aborts on the tensor layout.\r\n\r\nThat condition is pre-existing upstream behaviour rather than something this PR introduced (and the comment above it is already marked `TODO: move these checks to ggml_backend_sched`), so I mention it only because it affects anyone running this model on multiple GPUs — any MoE large enough to need expert offload loses pipeline parallelism, which is the case where it would help most. Happy to move that part to a separate discussion if it is out of scope here.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5458164455/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5554608359","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742#issuecomment-5554608359","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/27742","id":5554608359,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABSxSY5w","user":{"login":"fulvian","id":16386986,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2Mzg2OTg2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16386986?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fulvian","html_url":"https://github.com/fulvian","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fulvian/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fulvian/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fulvian/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fulvian/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fulvian/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fulvian/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fulvian/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fulvian/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fulvian/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-05T20:34:41Z","updated_at":"2026-09-05T20:34:41Z","body":"Related work, in case it is useful to people following the qwen4exp / PLE table support: we built a small tool that edits the PLE (Engram) table post-hoc to add a fact without touching the weights. The trigger's last three tokens address 16 rows; we optimize the 8 trigram-keyed rows by gradient through a CPU replica of the frozen model (routing refreshed every step) and ship them as an overlay that a fork of llama.cpp substitutes at gather time (`--ngram-on-disk` plus a `.pleo` overlay; the GGUF is never rewritten). On Qwen3.8-Flash-Next 7 of 8 facts come out of the quantized engine at first-token p 0.85–0.96; the replica matches the F32 engine on 17/17 grafts. What does not work: the fact stated inside a paragraph, and paraphrases. Code, run of record and a short report: https://github.com/fulvian/engraft-ngram. The engine changes are in a fork branch (`fork-ple`) referenced by commit; we will propose them upstream only once the PLE code here is stable.\n\nHow this was built: the code, the experiments and the write-up were produced in a Claude Code session (Anthropic's Claude, model Fable 5.1) driven by a single human operator who set the goals, approved every design step, ran the hardware and read every result. We are not after stars: we want the method checked, broken and improved.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/comments/5554608359/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]